# Expo app settings. Copy to .env and set the address of the Node backend. Read at bundle time as
# process.env.EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL. Never put secrets in EXPO_PUBLIC_* variables: they ship inside the app.
# (The backend has its own file, backend/.env, which holds TMDB_TOKEN and is never read by Expo.)
#
# Where the backend runs decides the address:
#   iOS simulator / Expo web ......... http://localhost:4000
#   Android emulator ................. http://10.0.2.2:4000
#   Physical phone (Expo Go) ......... http://<your computer's LAN IP>:4000   (same Wi-Fi as the computer)
#   Production ....................... https://your-api.example.com  (https is required for release builds)
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:4000
